From b557a581eea2f2c3354c6750cceff2c6bbf4a4eb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cascade Developer <developer@cascade.local>
Date: Mon, 6 Jul 2026 01:25:07 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(keyboard): defer KbScreen re-register out of the
 build phase (owner)

KbScreen.didUpdateWidget pushed to keyboardScreenToolsProvider SYNCHRONOUSLY
during the parent's build. For a screen whose tools list changes identity each
build (e.g. TasksScreen's live-count tree) this fired every rebuild, modifying
the provider mid-build. Debug throws _debugCanModifyProviders; in RELEASE (assert
stripped) the listener notifications inside buildScope corrupt the floating
keyboard's rebuild scheduling, so a later route pop no longer rebuilds it and the
live mirror STRANDS on the popped screen's tools ("dives in but not back out").

Defer the re-push to a microtask (as initState's post-frame push and dispose's
removeToken already do), with mounted guards so it is drop-safe if the screen
unmounts first. Flag-gated (kKbGlobal) so a flag-off build is byte-identical.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 app_flutter/lib/state/keyboard_screen_tools.dart | 16 +++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/app_flutter/lib/state/keyboard_screen_tools.dart b/app_flutter/lib/state/keyboard_screen_tools.dart
index 1b4a4ed4..c96c6fe8 100644
--- a/app_flutter/lib/state/keyboard_screen_tools.dart
+++ b/app_flutter/lib/state/keyboard_screen_tools.dart
@@ -234,7 +234,21 @@ class _KbScreenState extends ConsumerState<KbScreen> {
       // …).push` (a non-promotable field keeps its nullable type).
       final notifier = ref.read(keyboardScreenToolsProvider.notifier);
       _notifier = notifier;
-      notifier.push(KbScreenToolsEntry(_token, widget.tools));
+      final entry = KbScreenToolsEntry(_token, widget.tools);
+      // DEFER via microtask (mirrors [initState]'s post-frame push). didUpdateWidget
+      // runs DURING the parent's build (updateChild → update → didUpdateWidget), so
+      // pushing SYNCHRONOUSLY modifies [keyboardScreenToolsProvider] mid-build — an
+      // illegal provider mutation: debug throws `_debugCanModifyProviders`, and in
+      // RELEASE (assert stripped) it fires listener notifications inside `buildScope`
+      // that CORRUPT the floating keyboard's rebuild scheduling — after which a later
+      // route pop no longer rebuilds it and the mirror STRANDS on the popped screen's
+      // tools. This bit any screen whose `tools` list changes identity each build
+      // (e.g. TasksScreen's live-count tree). The microtask runs right after this
+      // build, when provider mutation is allowed; the `mounted` guards keep it
+      // drop-safe if the screen unmounts first (dispose's own removeToken wins).
+      Future.microtask(() {
+        if (mounted && notifier.mounted) notifier.push(entry);
+      });
     }
   }
 
